//==============================================================================
// add_pad : power / ground pads of mcu_pad_top (32-pad ring, 8 pads per side)
//   Included by mcu_pad_top.v at the end of the module (`include "add_pad").
//   Everything is commented out for now. When the power pads are needed
//   (PnR), remove the "//" marks. These cells have no signal ports.
//
//   Pad cells : PADVDD    core power        PADVSS    core ground
//               PADVDDIOR I/O ring power    PADVSSIOR I/O ring ground
//
//   Ring order (numbers follow the ring, counter-clockwise from the left side):
//     Left   : pad1  ~ pad8     Bottom : pad9  ~ pad16
//     Right  : pad17 ~ pad24    Top    : pad25 ~ pad32
//   Every side has the same pattern (position 1..8):
//     1 VSSIOR | 2 signal | 3 signal | 4 VDD | 5 VSS | 6 signal | 7 signal | 8 VDDIOR
//   The signal pads (positions 2, 3, 6, 7) are in mcu_pad_top.v.
//   Top side position 7 (pad31) has no signal: it holds a spare ground pad.
//   Total : 15 signal pads + 17 power pads (16 + 1 spare) = 32 pads.
//==============================================================================

